append(V/'docs/full-build-contract.md',r'''
## Interpreter representations and exact result projection

Normalized table rows have fixed structure: CSV/TSV {member,row,header,cells}, XLSX {member,sheet,row,cells:[{column,value,formula,cached_value}]}, XML {member,path,name,attributes,text,tail,children}, JSON/JSONL {member,row,value}, M2 sentence {member,sentence_index,text,tokens,edits} and edit {member,sentence_index,annotator,start,end,label,correction,raw}, TextGrid {member,tier,index,kind,start_seconds,end_seconds,label}, Kaldi {member,key,fields,raw}. Native scalar types/order and duplicate columns remain intact. XML expanded names use {namespaceURI}localName. Tables/record selectors address these defined parser outputs. Native identifiers remain in raw and group IDs; deterministic local IDs derive from source_id,release_id,member,table,native identity and actual row occurrence under JCS/SHA256. No synthetic learner identity is generated for missing source metadata.

A scalar projection locator reads one selected record or one exact one-join row; a many-joined locator cannot silently choose the first row. repeated_projections iterates all rows of its declared many-join table, applies its fields relative to that row into one object per element, and writes the complete array at to. Field targets inside an element are relative RFC6901 pointers. Conflicting output pointers/overwrites are mapping errors. Missing array values remain null with source absence retained; required invalid projections preserve the raw record but withhold its normalized candidate. For scalars, record/table references must be connected by the declared joins; unrelated rows never participate. Optional literal envelope fields (current local IDs/times/parser version/licence source metadata) are assigned by the native import owner under existing corpus-record rules, not copied from invented native annotations. Matching source_id/release_id/raw_manifest_sha256 is mandatory for applying a program. Source membership/completion is still the original selected release contract, not just the mapping table's members.

Completed rendering stores render-progress.sample_map_asset_id before final linkage. The private map is an ordered array of {piece_id,source_start,source_end,final_start,final_end,kind}; kind is copy,resample,duration,splice,pause or gap. Indexes are integer half-open intervals; inserted silence uses equal source_start/source_end. No copy/resample row may overlap final output of another row except a declared crossfade row with retained contributing pieces. A crossfade is represented by two splice rows and explicit shared final range. Assembly/duration length changes compute endpoints from actual returned sample counts. Phone/acoustic observations intersecting a splice retain that reason; they cannot pretend to be a clean source measurement.

For VOT landmark extraction, use the same source interval and24kHz clock: onset is the first three consecutive voiced10ms F0 frames after the initial stop release; require actual periodic pulses too. Search before that onset, inside the aligned stop interval, for the strongest positive10ms energy difference; its maximum-energy sample is the burst anchor. Keep the following5ms burst window; remove/extend only the interval from its end to the detected onset. If anchor/onset ordering is invalid, the interval is shorter than one actual period, or F0/pulse evidence is insufficient, return not_measurable with actual landmarks/reason; do not invent them. This deterministic landmark proposal is retained separately from acoustic interpretation and must be qualified against independent reference annotations during development. The zero-VOT default means no post-burst aspiration interval; reported measured VOT includes the retained burst definition and cannot be forced to zero by naming the request.

For explicit pitch-point recipes whose source median is not100Hz, resolve each listed relative default offset against the measured reference median before freezing the plan. Store the resolved100Hz-relative semitone targets in parameters.pitch_points. Thus a0-to5semitone default is a rise from the actual reference median, not a forced100Hz voice. A requested speech-rate duration ratio includes the final declared pause/gap denominator of that selected measurement interval: if total target length is60*spoken_token_count/target_WPM, subtract preserved silence length before dividing by source speech length. Nonpositive remaining speech duration is a constraint error. The output's actual WPM is measured separately, never populated by the formula's requested value.
''')
